venv/
logs/
lightning_logs/
checkpoints/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Secrets - never commit
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Large / generated
monitoring/bin/
artifacts/

# Corpora and caches. GitHub rejects any file over 100 MB, and these total
# ~526 MB — they are inputs that regenerate, not deliverables. The deployed
# services never read them: the backend serves PostgreSQL and the dashboard
# reads the small CSVs under outputs/ that ARE committed below.
#   reddit_hyperlinks.tsv          305 MB  (SNAP graph — download to rerun)
#   apollo_macro_embeddings_cache  179 MB  (regenerated by the macro layer)
#   apollo_comments.csv             41 MB  (rebuild: python simulate_data.py)
data/*.csv
data/*.tsv
!data/ground_truth.json
models/*.pt
models/*.pkl

# The one big output; the dashboard does not read it.
outputs/timeseries_with_embeddings.csv
outputs/*.png

# Stale or misleading artifacts — excluded so a deployment cannot serve them.
#   alerts_<timestamp>.json : 383 alerts, 100% CRITICAL, from the run that still
#       had the CHI x100 overflow. Contradicts the current 60-community outputs.
#       Live alerts are recomputed from meso_report.csv by the dashboard and the
#       exporter, so nothing depends on this file.
#   cybersecurity_anomalies.csv : synthetic Gaussian noise. CIC-IDS2017 is not in
#       this checkout, so the anomaly layer fell back to generated data — and the
#       layer is off-topic for a Reddit-community project either way.
#   community_health_report.csv / toxicity_by_subreddit_daily.csv : 383 and 2,143
#       rows of communities (r/0xProject, r/100yearsago...) that appear nowhere in
#       the current 60-community outputs. Superseded by meso_report.csv; shipping
#       them would put three different community sets in one repository.
outputs/alerts_*.json
outputs/cybersecurity_anomalies.csv
outputs/community_health_report.csv
outputs/toxicity_by_subreddit_daily.csv
main_run.log
*.log

#   live_feed.csv / live_stats.json : rewritten continuously by
#       ingest/live_replay.py while it runs, so tracking them means every git
#       operation collides with the replay. The Live page reports "replay idle"
#       when they are absent, which is the honest state on a deployment where
#       the replay is not running.
outputs/live_feed.csv
outputs/live_stats.json
